#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum atap ugārim šanītum pūssu santakkum
#tr.en: its first front is the ditch of the irrigation district, its second front is the triangular field;

8. _1(bur3)# 2(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_ puzur4-il3-a-ba4 i-ta nu-ur2-[i3-li2-szu sza _siki-hi-a_]
#tr.ts: ištēn būr šinā ikû eqlum ugārum puzur-ilaba itā nūr-ilīšu ša šīpātim
#tr.en: a field of 20 IKU in the Puzur-ilaba irrigation district next to (the field of) Nūr-ilīšu of the fleece (?)

9. u3# i-ta geme2-{d}utu u3 ni-szi-i-ni-szu _dumu-munus-mesz_ ah-hi a-[bi-sza]
#tr.ts: u itā amat-šamaš u nīši-īnīšu mārāt aḫḫī abīša
#tr.en: and next to (the field of) Amat-šamaš and Nīši-īnīšu, her (of Bēlessunu) cousins,

10. [_sag-bi] 1(disz)#-kam-ma_ a-tap _a-gar3 sag-bi-2(disz)-kam a-sza3_ [ur-{d}lugal-banda3{da}]
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum atap ugārim šanītum pūssu eqel ur-lugalbanda
#tr.en: its first front is the ditch of the irrigation district, its second front is the field of Ur-lugalbanda;

11. [_1(esze3) 3(iku) GAN2] a#-sza3 a-gar3_ ak-ba-ri i-ta mu-na-wi-[rum _dumu_ lu2-dingir]
#tr.ts: ištēn ebel šalāšat ikû eqlum ugārum akbari(m) itā muna(w)wirum mār awīl-ilī
#tr.en: a field of 9 IKU in the Akbarum irrigation district, next to (the field of) Munawwirum son of Awīl-ilī

12. [u3 i-ta {d}]suen#-i-qi2-sza-am _dumu_ {d}utu-kam u3 a-[sza3 lukur_ {d}utu]
#tr.ts: u itā sîn-iqīšam mār šamaš-kam u eqel nadīt šamaš
#tr.en: and next to (the field of) Sîn-iqīšam son of Šamaš-kam and the field of the Šamaš’s nadītu

13. [sza i-ta {d}suen]-eri#-ba-am _dumu_ dumu-zimbir{ki}
#tr.ts: ša itā sîn-erībam mār mār-sippir
#tr.en: that is next to (the field of) Sîn-erībam son of Mār-sippar,

14. [_sag-bi 1(disz)-kam-ma_ {i7}nu]-ra#-tum _sag-bi 2(disz)-kam e_ sa-mu#-[um]
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum nūratum šanītum pūssu īki samum
#tr.en: its first front is the (canal) Nūratum, its second front is the dike Samum,

15. [_usz 1(disz)]-kam-ma ib? im usz 2(disz)-kam-ma [...]
#tr.ts: šiddum maḫrûm ... šanûm šiddum ...
#tr.en: the first edge is ... the second edge is ...;

16. [_2(esze3)] GAN2# a-sza3 a-gar3_ pa!(IRI)-hu#-[s,um{ki}]
#tr.ts: šinā ebel eqlum ugārum paḫuṣum
#tr.en: a field of 12 IKU in the Paḫuṣum irrigation district;

17. [_1(disz) 1/3(disz) sar e2 du3-a] u3 ki-gal2_ i-na ga2-gi-im
#tr.ts: ištēn šaluš mūšar bītum epšum u maškanum ina gagîm
#tr.en: a built house and an unbuilt plot of 80 shekels in the cloister

18. [_da e2_ geme2]-ka-al-la-tim u3 _da e2 dumu-munus#_ [da-qum]
#tr.ts: ṭēḫi bīt amat-kallatim u ṭēḫi bīt mārat da(q)qum
#tr.en: adjacent to the house of Amat-kallatum and adjacent to the house of Daqqum’s daughter;

19. _6(disz) sar# [e2 ki]-gal2_ i-na zimbir{ki}-gal i-na _sila [{d}imin-bi_]
#tr.ts: šeššet mūšar maškanum ina sippir-rabûm ina sūqu sebettum
#tr.en: an unbuilt plot of 6 SAR in the "Great Sippar", in the street "The Seven (gods)";

20. _1(disz) sag-nita2_ {d}suen-ma-asz-ma-asz u3 _1(disz) sag-nita2 dumu-mesz_ [...]
#tr.ts: ištēn wardum sîn-mašmaš u ištēn wardum mārū ...
#tr.en: a male slave (named) Sîn-mašmaš and a male slave, sons ...;

21. _1(disz) sag-nita2_ a-na-pa-ni-{d}utu-na-di _aszgab#_ x [...]
#tr.ts: ištēn wardum ana-pānī-šamaš-nadi aškāpum ...
#tr.en: a male slave (named) Ana-pānī-šamaš-nadi leatherworker ...;

22. _2(disz) {uruda}szen-hi-a_ mi-im-ma an#-[nu-um bu]-szu#-sza# [wa-ar-ka-sa3]
#tr.ts: šinā ruqqū mimma annûm būšūša warka(s)sa
#tr.en: 2 copper cauldrons; all this, her properties (and) her inherited possessions,

23. s,u2-lu-sza sza i-na i-ga-ri#-[im za-aq-pa-at]
#tr.ts: ṣu(l)lûša ša ina igārim zaqpat
#tr.en: her pin is stuck into the wall,

24. isz-tu pe2-e a-di _ku3-sig17_ sza be-[le-su2-nu _dumu-munus_ ma-ni-um]
#tr.ts: ištu pê adi ḫurāṣim ša bēle(s)sunu mārat manium
#tr.en: everything that is Bēlessunu's, daughter of Manûm,

25. sza a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu-ma _dumu-munus_ {d}suen-dingir a-pil#-[ti-sza]
#tr.ts: ša amat-māmūma mārat sîn-ilī apiltīša
#tr.en: belongs to Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī, her heiress.

26. a-di be-le-su2-nu ba-al-t,a3-at mi-im-ma!(mu)-sza
#tr.ts: adi bēle(s)sunu balṭat mimmâša
#tr.en: As long as Bēlessunu lives, her property

27. qa2-ti {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu-ma u2-ka-al-ma
#tr.ts: qāti amat-māmūma ukālma
#tr.en: Amat-šamaš will hold and

28. i-na _mu 1(disz)-kam 6(asz) sze gur 1(u) 2(disz) ma-na siki-hi-a <2(ban2)> 4(disz) [sila3 i3-ba_]
#tr.ts: ina ištēt šattim šeššet kur še’am šinšeret manā šīpātim šitta šât ešret qa piššatam
#tr.en: every year: 1.800 litres of barley, 12 minas of wool allowance, 24 litres of oil allotment,

29. 6(disz) ezem-hi-a 2(ban2) zi3-da-ta-a u3 2(disz) uzu-ta-a#_
#tr.ts: šeššet isinnī šitta šât qēmam u šinā šīrī
#tr.en: 6 "isinnu" food portions, 20 litres of flour and 2 thigh-cuts of meat,

30. {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu a-na be-le-su2-nu i-na-ad-di#-[isz-szi-im]
#tr.ts: amat-māmu ana bēle(s)sunu inaddiššim
#tr.en: Amat-māmu to Bēlessunu will provide her.

31. _2/3(disz) ma-na 6(disz) gin2 ku3-babbar_ hu-bu-li be-le-su2-nu
#tr.ts: šinip manā šeššet šiqil kaspam ḫubu(l)li bēle(s)sunu
#tr.en: 46 shekels of silver, a debt of Bēlessunu,

32. {disz}a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ {d}suen-dingir i-pu-ul
#tr.ts: amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilī īpul
#tr.en: Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī paid (so)

33. {disz}be-le-su2-nu u2-ul ih-ta-ba-al
#tr.ts: bēle(s)sunu ul iḫtabal
#tr.en: Bēlessunu is no (more) in debt.

34. mi-im-mu-sza an-nu-um a-na hu-bu-li-sza u2-ul iz-za-az
#tr.ts: mimmûša annûm ana ḫubu(l)līša ul izzaz
#tr.en: All her (aforementioned) property will not be liable for her debt (and)

35. sza sze-a-am u3 _ku3-babbar_ i-qi2-ip-pu-szi i-na mi-im-mu-sza# i-te-el-li
#tr.ts: ša še’am ū kaspam iqippūši ina mimmûša ītelli
#tr.en: whoever would lend barley or silver to her, would have no right to (lit. will forfeit) her property.

36. isz-tu be-le-su2-nu ap-lu-sa3 an-ni-tam
#tr.ts: ištu bēle(s)sunu aplū(s)sa annîtam
#tr.en: After Bēlessunu this inheritance

37. a-na a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu id-di-nu-ma _mu 2(disz)-kam_ i-pe2-ru-szi
#tr.ts: ana amat-māmu iddinūma šittā šanātim īpirūši
#tr.en: to Amat-māmu gave and supported her for two years,

38. {disz}geme2-{d}utu _dumu-munus_ i3-li2-i-qi2-sza-am u3 ni-szi-i-ni-szu _dumu-munus_ dingir-pi4-{d}utu
#tr.ts: amat-šamaš mārat ilī-iqīšam u nīši-īnīšu mārat anum-pî-šamaš
#tr.en: Amat-šamaš daughter of Ilī-iqīšam and Nīši-īnīšu daughter of Anum-pî-šamaš,

39. _dumu-munus-mesz_ ah-hi a-bi-sza a-na _a-sza3_ sza pi2-i t,up-pi2 an-ni-im
#tr.ts: mārāt aḫḫī abīša ana eqlim ša pî tuppi(m) annîm
#tr.en: her cousins, for the field(s) which are reported in this tablet,

40. a#-na# be-le-su2-nu ir-gu-ma-ma
#tr.ts: ana bēle(s)sunu irgumāma
#tr.en: raised a claim against Bēlessunu.

41. {disz}zi-im-ri-e-ra-ah ra-bi-a-an zimbir#{[ki]}
#tr.ts: zimri-eraḫ rabiān sippir
#tr.en: Zimri-eraḫ, the mayor of Sippar,

42. u3# _kar_ zimbir{ki} i-na _ka2_ {d}utu i#-mu#-ru#-[ma]
#tr.ts: u kār sippir ina bāb šamaš īmurūma
#tr.en: and the kārum body of Sippar investigated (the case) at the gate of Šamaš and:

43. t,up-pa-at nu-du-ne2-e be-le-su2-nu _lukur_ {d}utu
#tr.ts: ṭuppāt nudu(n)nê bēle(s)sunu nadīt šamaš
#tr.en: the tablets concerning the dowry of Bēlessunu nadītu of Šamaš,

44. sza a-bu-sza ma-la _sza3_-sza u2-sza-am-s,u2-u2-szi
#tr.ts: ša abūša mala libbīša ušamṣūši
#tr.en: which her father had conceded her full discretion over;

45. t,up#-pa#-at ap-lu-ut na-ra-am-tum a-ha-at a-bi-sza
#tr.ts: ṭuppāt aplūt narāmtum aḫat abīša
#tr.en: the inheritance tablets of Narāmtum her aunt,

46. [sza ap]-lu-sa3 id-di-nu-szi-im-ma
#tr.ts: ša aplū(s)sa iddinūšimma
#tr.en: who had given her inheritance to her and (who)

47. [e-ma] e#-li-sza t,a3-bu ap-lu-sa3 na-da-nam isz-t,u2-ru-szi
#tr.ts: ēma elīša ṭābu aplū(s)sa nadanam išṭurūši
#tr.en: had put in writing that she would place her inheritance wherever was good for her,

@reverse
1. u3 t,up-pa-at _dumu-munus-mesz_ ah-hi a-bi-sza sza ir-gu-ma-szi-im
#tr.ts: u ṭuppāt mārāt aḫḫī abīša ša irgumāšim
#tr.en: as well as the tablets of her cousins who sued her,

2. i-mu-ru-u2-ma a-na pi4 t,up-pa-ti-sza mi-im-ma-sza an-ni-a-am
#tr.ts: īmurūma ana pî ṭuppātīša mimmâša annîam
#tr.en: examined and, according to the content of her tablets, all her estate

3. a-na [be]-le-su2-nu-ma u2-bi-ir-ru
#tr.ts: ana bēle(s)sunūma ubirrū
#tr.en: they confirmed to Bēlessunu.

4. asz-szum {disz}geme2-{d}utu u3 ni-szi-i-ni-szu i-na la i-di-im ir-gu-ma-szi
#tr.ts: aššum amat-māmu u nīši-īnīšu ina la idim irgumāši(m)
#tr.en: Because Amat-šamaš and Nīši-īnīšu brought a suit against her whitout grounds,

5. sze-ri-it {d}utu i-mi-du-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: šerit šamaš īmidūšināti
#tr.en: (the judges) imposed the penalty of Šamaš to them

6. u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im u2-sze-zi-bu-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: u ṭuppi la ragamim ušezibūšināti
#tr.en: and had them make out a no-claim tablet.

7. isz-tu t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im u2-sze-zi-bu-szi-na-ti
#tr.ts: ištu ṭuppi la ragamim ušezibūšināti
#tr.en: After (the judges) had them make out the no-claim tablet,

8. u3 be-le-su2-nu a-na szi-ma-ti-sza il-li-ku
#tr.ts: u bēle(s)sunu ana šimatīša illiku
#tr.en: and Bēlessunu died,

9. t,up-pi2 ap-lu-tim t,up-pa-at um-ma-tim sza _a-sza3 u3 e2_
#tr.ts: ṭuppi aplūtim ṭuppāt ummatim ša eqlim u bītim
#tr.en: the tablet of inheritance, the original tablets concerning the field(s) and the house

10. sza be-le-su2-nu a-na a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ sin-dingir id-di-nu
#tr.ts: ša bēle(s)sunu ana amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilī iddinu
#tr.en: that Bēlessunu had given to Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī

11. u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im sza _dumu-munus-mesz ah-hi a-bi-sza szu-zu-ba
#tr.ts: u ṭuppi la ragamim ša mārāt aḫḫī abīša šuzubā
#tr.en: as well as the no-claim tablet that her cousins had had to leave,

12. {disz}{d}suen-dingir a-na _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen# a-hi-sza
#tr.ts: sîn-ilī ana bīt ikūn-pî-sîn ahīša
#tr.en: Sîn-ilī into the house of Ikūn-pî-sîn his brother

13. a-na ma-s,a-ar-tim i-zi-ba t,up-[pa-tum szi-na]
#tr.ts: ana ma(ṣ)ṣartim īziba(m) ṭuppātum šina
#tr.en: brought for safekeeping. These tablets

14. i-na _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen ih-li#-[qa2-ma]
#tr.ts: ina bīt ikūn-pî-sîn iḫliqāma
#tr.en: were lost in the house of Ikūn-pî-sîn so

15. {disz}sin-dingir ma-har {d}suen-isz-me-[a-ni]
#tr.ts: sîn-ilī maḫar sîn-ismea(n)ni
#tr.en: Sîn-ilī before Sîn-išmeanni

16. u3 _kar zimbir{ki}_ isz-ku-ma# [ki-ma t,up-pa-tum szi-na hal-qa2-a]
#tr.ts: u kār sippir išku(m)ma kīma ṭuppātum šina ḫalqā
#tr.en: and the kāru body of Sippar has made a statement and: "These tablets have been lost!"

17. i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen a-na {d}suen#-[isz-me-a-ni u3 _kar_ zimbir{ki} iq-bi]
#tr.ts: ikūn-pî-sîn ana sîn-ismeanni u kār sippir iqbi
#tr.en: Ikūn-pî-sîn has said to Sîn-išmeanni and the kāru body of Sippar.

18. [i]-na# qa2-be2-e {disz}{d}suen-isz-me-a-[ni u3 _kar_ zimbir{ki}]
#tr.ts: ina qabê sîn-ismeanni u kār sippir
#tr.en: By order of Sîn-išmeanni and the kāru body of Sippar,

19. [t,up]-pa-szu an-ni-a-am a-na pi2-i szi-[bu-tim u2-ba-al-li-t,u2-ma]
#tr.ts: ṭuppašu annîam ana pî šībūtim uballiṭūma
#tr.en: they have let this relevant tablet drawn up according to the testimony of the witnesses so (if)
#For ṭuppa-šu, see K. R. Veenhof in "Figurative Language in the Ancient Near East" London, 1987 p. 62 n. 31.

20. [t,up]-pi2 ap-lu-tim t,up-pa-at um-[ma-tim u3 t,up-pi2 la ra-ga-mi-im]
#tr.ts: ṭuppi aplūtim ṭuppāt ummatim u ṭuppi la ragamim
#tr.en: the tablet of inheritance, the original tablets and the no-claim tablet,

21. [sza] a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu _dumu-munus_ {d}suen#-[dingir it-ti be-le-su2-nu la-qi2-a-at]
#tr.ts: ša amat-māmu mārat sîn-ilî itti bēle(s)sunu laqiat
#tr.en: which Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī acquired from Bēlessunu,

22. [i]-na# _e2_ i-ku-un-pi4-{d}suen [u3 e-ma in-nam-ma-ra]
#tr.ts: ina bīt ikūn-pî-sîn u ēma innammarā
#tr.en: should be found in Ikūn-pî-sîn’s house or wherever,

23. [sza] a-ma-at-{d}ma-mu-ma# [_dumu-munus_ {d}suen-dingir ...]
#tr.ts: ša amat-māmūma mārat sîn-ilī
#tr.en: are of Amat-māmu daughter of Sîn-ilī alone

