&P512341 = BAP 042 
#atf: lang akk 
@tablet 
@obverse 
1. _2(bur3) 1(esze3) 3(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 a-gar3_ a-mu-ur-ri-i{ki} 
#tr.ts: šinā būr ištēn ebel šalašat ikû eqel ugār amurrī
#tr.en: A field of 43 IKU in (lit. of) the Amorites' irrigation district,

2. szi-ma-at ib-ni-{d}iszkur _ugula dam-gar3_ 
#tr.ts: šīmāt ibni-adad akil tamkarim
#tr.en: the property purchased by (lit. of) Ibni-adad overseer of the merchant(s),

3. {disz}ARAD2-{d}suen _dumu_ e-t,e-rum 
#tr.ts: warad-sîn mār eṭerum
#tr.en: Warad-sîn son of Eṭerum

4. ma-har _di-ku5-mesz_ ki-a-am id-bu-ub 
#tr.ts: maḫār dayyānī kīam idbub
#tr.en: before the judges thus he pleaded (his case)

5. um-ma szu-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: umma šūma
#tr.en: as follows:

6. _a-sza3_-um sza it-ti _e2_ a-bi-ia la sza-a-mu 
#tr.ts: eqlum ša itti bīt abīya lā šâmu
#tr.en: "The field that is from my father’s house was not purchased;

7. {disz}ip-qu2-{d}sza-la u3 ah-hu-szu _dumu-mesz_ {d}utu-na-s,i-ir 
#tr.ts: ipqu-šala u aḫḫūšu mārū šamaš-nāṣir
#tr.en: Ipqu-šala and his brothers, sons of Šamaš-nāṣir,

8. a-na ib-ni-{d}iszkur _ugula dam-gar3_ 
#tr.ts: ana ibni-adad akil tamkarim
#tr.en: to Ibni-adad the overseer of the merchant(s)

9. a-na _ku3-babbar_-im it-ta-ad-nu 
#tr.ts: ana kaspim ittadnū
#tr.en: they sold (lit. gave for silver).”.

10. {disz}id-da-tum u3 ba-zi-zum 
#tr.ts: iddatum u bazizum
#tr.en: Iddatum and Bazizum,

11. _dumu-mesz_ ib-ni-{d}iszkur _ugula dam-gar3_ 
#tr.ts: mārū ibni-adad akil tamkarim
#tr.en: sons of Ibni-adad the overseer of the merchant(s),

12. a-na ma-har _di-ku5-mesz_ u2-qe2-er-ri-bu-ni-isz-szu-nu-ti 
#tr.ts: ana maḫar dayyānī uqerribūniššunuti
#tr.en: were produced before the judges

13. a-wa-ti-szu-nu i-mu-ru 
#tr.ts: awātīšunu īmurū
#tr.en: (who) examined their case.

14. a-na pi2-i tup-pi2 szi-ma-a-tim 
#tr.ts: ana pî ṭuppi šīmātim
#tr.en: According to the wording of the purchase document,

15. sza e-t,e-rum u3 {d}suen-na-di-in-szu-mi 
#tr.ts: ša eṭerum u sîn-nādin-šumī
#tr.en: (stating) that Eṭerum u Sîn-nādin-šumī

16. a-na {d}utu-na-s,i-ir 
#tr.ts: ana šamaš-nāṣir
#tr.en: to Šamaš-nāṣir

17. u3 ip-qu2-an-nu-ni-tum 
#tr.ts: u ipqu-annunītum
#tr.en: and Ipqu-annunītum

18. ma-ri-szu 
#tr.ts: mārīšu
#tr.en: his son

@reverse 
1. a-na _ku3-babbar_ id-di-nu 
#tr.ts: ana kaspim iddinū
#tr.en: had sold

2. _2(bur3) 2(iku) GAN2 a-sza3 sza3 3(bur3) GAN2 a-sza3_ sza sza-ne2-e
#So Schörr in UAZP n. 269. Meissner reads a-sza3 il?-ta?-ni-e.
#tr.ts: šinā būr šinā ikû eqlam libbum šalašat būr eqlim ša šanê
#tr.en: a field of 38 IKU inside the field of 54 IKU of someone else 

3. u3 _1(esze3) 1(iku) GAN2 4(u)? sar a-sza3_ sza _a-gar3_ a-mu-ur-ri-i 
#tr.ts: u ištēn ebel ištēn ikû erbā mūšar eqlam ša ugār amurrī
#tr.en: and a field of 740 SAR in the Amorites' irrigation district,

4. _sag-bi 1(disz) a-sza3_ i3-li2-ma-lu-sze-SZI 
#tr.ts: pūssu maḫrītum ilīma-lušeši
#tr.en: its first front is (the property of) Ilīma-lušeši,

5. _sag-bi 2(disz)-kam-ma i7_ bu-sza-a-tum 
#tr.ts: šanītum pūssu nār bušatum
#tr.en: its second front is the canal Bušatum,

6. si!-ka!-at _a-sza3_ im-ma-ha-s,a-am-ma 
#tr.ts: si(k)kat eqlim imma(ḫ)ḫaṣamma
#tr.en: the border marker (lit. peg) of the field will be driven in and

7. il-la-qe2-a-am 
#tr.ts: illa(q)qeam
#tr.en: will be taken over.

8. a-na ARAD2-{d}suen _dumu_ e-t,e-rum iq-bu-u2 
#tr.ts: ana warad-sîn mār eṭerum iqbū
#tr.en: (This is what) was declared to Warad-sîn son of Eṭerum.

9. i-na e-re-eb zimbir{ki} _a-sza3_-am i-sza-ad-da-du-u2-ma 
#tr.ts: ina ereb sippar eqlam išaddadūma
#tr.en: At the entrance of Sippar, they will measure the field and,

10. a-na pi2-i tup-pi2 szi-ma-tim sza {d}utu-na-s,i-ir 
#tr.ts: ana pî ṭuppi šīmātim ša šamaš-nāṣir
#tr.en: on the basis of the purchase document belonging to Šamaš-nāṣir

11. u3 ip-qu2-an-nu-ni-tum ma-ri-szu 
#tr.ts: u ipqu-annunītum mārīšu
#tr.en: and Ipqu-annunītum his son,

12. {disz}ARAD2-{d}suen _dumu_ e-t,e-rum _{gesz}gag_ i-ma-ah-ha-as,-ma 
#tr.ts: warad-sîn mār eṭerum sikkatam imaḫḫaṣma
#tr.en: Warad-sîn son of Eṭerum will plant the peg and

13. IL _a-sza3_-szu i-le-eq-qe2 
#tr.ts: el(i) eqlīšu ileqqe
#tr.en: will take his field.

$ single ruling 
14. _igi_ {d}nanna-ma-an-szum2 _di-ku5_ 
#tr.ts: maḫār nanna-manšum dayyānim
#tr.en: Before Nanna-manšum, judge;

15. _igi_ {d}suen-isz-me-a-ni _di-ku5_ 
#tr.ts: maḫār sîn-išmean(n)i dayyānim
#tr.en: before Sîn-išmeanni, judge;

16. _igi_ ip-qu2-an-nu-ni-tum _di-ku5_ 
#tr.ts: maḫār ipqu-annunītum dayyānim
#tr.en: before Ipqu-annunītum, judge;

17. _igi_ ip-qu2-i3-li2-szu _di-ku5_ 
#tr.ts: maḫār ipqu-ilīšu dayyānim
#tr.en: before Ipqu-ilīšu, judge.

$ single ruling 
18. _iti szu-numun-a u4 6(disz)-kam_ 
#tr.ts: waraḫ dumuzi ūmam šeššet
#tr.en: The month of Dumuzi, the day 6,

19. _mu_ am-mi-s,a-du-qa2 _lugal-e {uruda}du8 mah gal-gal-la hur-sag i7-da# ib2#?-diri#-ga e2# nam-ti-la-sze3 in-ne-en-ku4-ra_
#tr.ts: šattum ša ammi-ṣaduqa šarrum dâm ṣīram rabiam ḫuršānī nārātim atrūtim ina enamtila ušēribu
#tr.en: the year in which Ammi-ṣaduqa the king brought into Entamila a splendid great platform (depicting) mountains and rivers which were numerous.

